fhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2365e5320559893c6deca447bee47321e5705d37bb97d7b208912a09f50469cd","event_uuid":"14ab50af-0b17-4630-a7a4-997adaec1907","position":{"commit_sha":"733759628b5c45f643e5eefcdfeac067b54afbfb","position":"1787358793435495001-14ab50af-0b17-4630-a7a4-997adaec1907"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"202f08c1fde487d9ea410302e886320c83bf9effa75ceb04cda7a9762852986d","event_uuid":"80c9cadc-cdc1-4401-8cec-3a8c6ba44ba8","position":{"commit_sha":"4e994b27484ae7b09713311a4f942c4ebc0ff56e","position":"1787359002340732001-80c9cadc-cdc1-4401-8cec-3a8c6ba44ba8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented the compact-worker leg in scan_locks via the existing _existence_report helper, keyed on the canonicalised tracker's .rebar/ (inherits fix 13f78e3165's canonical-store keying — scan_locks canonicalises before deriving rebar_dir, exactly as compact_trigger does). Module docstring census updated to five legs. Tests: free store reports the leg free with no spurious holder; live-holder lock is info (named, aged, pid live, no finding); dead-holder lock is a stale-lock finding. RED confirmed before the edit (3 failures on the four-leg census), GREEN after; lint/typecheck/complexity ratchet green. NOTE on adjacent scope: snapshot GC (a3da2f4cce) added <snapshot-store>/gc/worker.lock — same detached-worker shape, but it lives on a different root (the snapshot store, not the tracker's .rebar/), so it needs its own root-derivation/staleness design. Filed as unanimated-detectible-cow (2b09-d231-2152-42d6, discovered_from this ticket) rather than scope-creeping here.","timestamp":1787354674431736001}],"created_at":1787309327931304001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a95488a3-08e9-4bea-97ec-8cdfc764cffd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"93a9-66cf-e681-4f49"},{"link_uuid":"e3038c02-f645-44f0-a0ba-1b169a5d99dd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d64d-bc57-fe56-4b5f"},{"link_uuid":"2397c116-3773-4dd8-a55f-9bf49cf09d56","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7266-c515-3592-476b"}],"description":"## Context\n\nFound by the Step-7 parity sweep of bug `intangible-ladyish-vicuna` (`93a9-66cf-e681-4f49`),\nwhich restored the compaction trigger's sidecars to the canonical store.\n\n`doctor_locks.scan_locks` (`src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py`) canonicalises the tracker\n(`_lock.canonical_tracker`) and then reports four legs — `tickets-write-fcntl`,\n`tickets-write-mkdir`, `hlc`, `enrich-drain`. There is NO leg for `compact-worker.lock`, even\nthough it is a stamped advisory lock in the same `.rebar/`\n(`compact_trigger._TRIGGER_LOCK_NAME = \"compact-worker.lock\"`, derived from the CANONICAL\ntracker per fix 13f78e3165 / `intangible-ladyish-vicuna`), arbitrated by the same\n`lock_owner.stamped_file_is_stale` decision table as the drain lock next to it.\n\nConsequence: a compaction worker that dies between acquire and release leaves a stamped lock\nthat `rebar doctor` cannot see, so the one diagnostic built to answer \"who holds what\" is\nsilent about the lock most likely to be held by a detached background process. (The lock IS\nself-healing via the shared staleness table, so this is observability, not correctness.)\n\nNote: the `intangible-ladyish-vicuna` description asserted that \"`rebar doctor` describes the\ncanonical `compact-worker.lock`\". It does not — that assumption was checked and disproved\nduring the debug session, which is what surfaced this gap.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd a `compact-worker` leg to `scan_locks` alongside `enrich-drain`, reusing the existing\nstamped-file report helper `_existence_report` (the compact-worker lock is the same\n`O_EXCL`-file-with-v2-stamp shape as the drain lock — `compact_trigger` reuses the drain's\nmachinery by design). Deliberately NOT done inside the bug fix: adding a doctor leg is\nnew capability, and that fix was held to restoration only.\n\nOut of scope: snapshot GC's `<store>/gc/worker.lock` (a3da2f4cce) lives in the snapshot\nstore, not the tracker's `.rebar/`, and gets its own discovered_from ticket rather than\nscope-creeping here.\n\n## Plan (exact edit set)\n\nIn `src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py`:\n1. Add `LEG_COMPACT_WORKER = \"compact-worker\"` beside the other leg-name constants and\n   `_COMPACT_WORKER_LOCK_NAME = \"compact-worker.lock\"` beside `_DRAIN_LOCK_NAME` (kept as a\n   local constant, matching how `_DRAIN_LOCK_NAME` mirrors `enrich_drain`'s name rather than\n   importing across packages).\n2. Add a fifth leg tuple to `scan_locks`, directly after `enrich-drain`:\n   `_existence_report(LEG_COMPACT_WORKER, os.path.join(rebar_dir, _COMPACT_WORKER_LOCK_NAME),\n   note=...)`. `rebar_dir` is already derived from the CANONICALISED tracker at the top of\n   `scan_locks`, so the leg inherits the canonical-store keying the compact trigger itself\n   uses (fix 13f78e3165) with no new path logic.\n3a. Admit the new leg in `src/rebar/schemas/doctor.schema.json` — the doctor output\n   schema enumerates the lock-leg names, so the census gains `compact-worker` there too\n   (surfaced by the schema-validation test in CI).\n3. Update the module docstring's leg census (\"Four legs are reported\" → five, naming\n   `.rebar/compact-worker.lock` as a second stamped existence lock).\n\nIn `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py` (the doctor-locks test module — the\n`tests/unit/` path originally recorded on this ticket does not exist):\n4. Extend `test_a_free_store_reports_every_leg_and_no_finding` to include\n   `LEG_COMPACT_WORKER` in the expected leg-name set and assert its state is `free` with no\n   holder (the free store must not report a spurious holder).\n5. Add held-leg tests mirroring the drain-lock ones, via a `_plant_compact_lock` helper\n   parallel to `_plant_drain_lock`:\n   - a live-holder compact-worker lock reads `held`, names this pid, `pid_state == \"live\"`,\n     `not-stale`, and produces NO finding;\n   - a dead-holder compact-worker lock reads `stale` and IS a `stale-lock` finding.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\n- RED first: the new/extended tests fail against the current four-leg census (missing leg),\n  then GREEN after the edit.\n- `pytest tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py -q` green.\n- `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` green\n  (`scan_locks` grows one data tuple, not a branch, so its McCabe score is unchanged).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `rebar doctor` reports a `compact-worker` lock leg, on the canonical store, with the\n      same held-for / staleness / holder detail the `enrich-drain` leg carries.\n- [x] A test covers a held compact-worker lock appearing in the census (live holder → info,\n      dead holder → stale finding).\n- [x] A test covers a free store not reporting a spurious compact-worker holder.\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, complexity ratchet and the unit sweep green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py","reason":"add the compact-worker lock leg to the census"},{"path":"tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py","reason":"cover the new leg held and free (this is the doctor-locks test module; tests/unit/test_doctor_locks.py does not exist)"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/doctor.schema.json","reason":"the doctor output schema enumerates lock leg names; the new compact-worker leg must be admitted there"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7266-c515-3592-476b"],["relates_to","d64d-bc57-fe56-4b5f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"668f6a03-4a0a-49b3-8822-e1ad504fe8f8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8a0d-96ca-a60e-4da6","ticket_type":"task","title":"doctor's lock census has no compact-worker leg","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["38959e50-e77e-4dcc-8c25-de7f1d4fc5df","51250540-277e-488a-be11-f7f41884cc24","609408e7-ce2c-4bde-8176-a23fdf396fec","668f6a03-4a0a-49b3-8822-e1ad504fe8f8","7b18cea8-4a14-4825-afaa-b0526c1152d3","eb90571e-e6a5-4646-80c5-94f658d3f308","e3038c02-f645-44f0-a0ba-1b169a5d99dd","2397c116-3773-4dd8-a55f-9bf49cf09d56","a71613be-8783-40ae-86f4-4a037f8f859e","10dfa2d6-d133-4a1c-adb7-d041a0e29c46","14ab50af-0b17-4630-a7a4-997adaec1907","80c9cadc-cdc1-4401-8cec-3a8c6ba44ba8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787359002340732002,"uuid":"33f6f8c5-a2f6-491f-a3ac-e176cc6da120"}